<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Payroll Processing?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>End-to-end monthly cycle: gross salary from CTC, statutory deductions (EPF/ESI/TDS), reimbursements, net pay, bank disbursement, payslips, statutory deposits, and records. Management adds CTC structuring, compliance calendar, investment proofs, Form 16, F&amp;F, and audit support. For <a href="/tds-return-filing-24q">TDS Return Filing</a>, see our page.</p>
                    <p>For Gurugram: 50% wage rule restructuring, dual tax regime, and industry-specific tracks (ESOP, shifts, service charge, trips, trust, FCRA). Payroll integrated with accounting = one team. For <a href="/accounting-services/gurugram">Accounting Services Gurugram</a>, see our page.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Payroll Processing:</strong></p>
                    <ul><li><strong>50% Wage Rule:</strong> Basic min 50% CTC (SSC 2020). PF base increases Rs 1,500-5,000/emp/month</li><li><strong>EPF ECR:</strong> Monthly PF filing EPFO Gurugram. 12%+12%. Due 15th. Late = 1%/month + 25% damages</li><li><strong>Dual Regime:</strong> Old (80C/HRA deductions) vs new (lower rates). Per employee. Year-end adjustment</li><li><strong>F&amp;F:</strong> Exit settlement within 2 days per Code on Wages. Gratuity, leave, bonus, PF transfer</li><li><strong>Form 16:</strong> Annual TDS certificate. Part A + Part B. Due June 15. Prevents employee ITR errors</li><li><strong>No PT:</strong> Haryana advantage. Rs 12.5L/year saved for 500 employees vs Mumbai</li></ul>

                </div>
            </div>
